        data-v-b2e27a45=""
      >
        <strong
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          Surface profile
        </strong>
        <p
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          The profile function and Snell calculation are selected as a single physical model.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        data-v-b2e27a45=""
      >
        <strong
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          Bezel ratio
        </strong>
        <p
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          The ratio is measured against the corner radius, or half of the short side when the radius is zero.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        data-v-b2e27a45=""
      >
        <strong
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          Selected item glass
        </strong>
        <p
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          The active item owns one size-matched filter, reuses the optical tuning and releases it when selection moves.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        data-v-b2e27a45=""
      >
        <strong
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          RGBA displacement encoding
        </strong>
        <p
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          R/G displacement and alpha clipping remain an internal filter contract.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        data-v-b2e27a45=""
      >
        <strong
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          SVG filter graph
        </strong>
        <p
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          Blur, displacement, saturation, masked specular and blend order are validated together.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        data-v-b2e27a45=""
      >
        <strong
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          512K adaptive budget
        </strong>
        <p
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          Sampling dimensions are resolved together to preserve aspect ratio and memory limits.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article
        data-v-b2e27a45=""
      >
        <strong
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          CSS fallback ladder
        </strong>
        <p
          data-v-b2e27a45=""
        >
          Capability failure must retain the same readable baseline and interaction surface.
        </p>
      </article>
      
    </div>
  </section>
</section>
`;

